WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.660
- Your accent reminds me of home.

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:03.530
I always love when I run into you.

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.450
It just feels, so where did you grow up?

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:07.630
- I grew up in North Carolina.
- North Carolina?

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:09.690
- My mom made be a debutante, that's how

00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.160
Southern I am.
- You're a Southern belle.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:12.710
- I am.
- You're a Southern belle.

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:14.550
Wait, what did that entail,
what did you have to do?

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:16.160
Oh, my gosh!
- Ooh!

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.770
- I was like, "What happened!"

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.690
(all laughing)

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:22.130
- You are so fancy right now!

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:22.963
- [Fortune] Y'all, I had to wear

00:00:22.963 --> 00:00:24.100
a white wedding gown.
- Oh my God,

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.460
you are from like the bricks,

00:00:25.460 --> 00:00:26.460
I was from the sticks, girl.

00:00:26.460 --> 00:00:27.570
We didn't have anything like that.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:30.910
- Listen, but we had no
money, that was the thing.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:34.150
My mom had been one and
then we lost all our money.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:35.230
(Kelly laughs)
It happens.

00:00:35.230 --> 00:00:36.090
- It happens.

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:38.566
- You know, gambling.

00:00:38.566 --> 00:00:40.697
(all laughing)

00:00:40.697 --> 00:00:42.640
And then she still wanted me

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.200
to carry on this tradition of being,

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.740
pretending to be rich and
then go to etiquette classes.

00:00:49.740 --> 00:00:51.015
- That's amazing.
- Etiquette classes?

00:00:51.015 --> 00:00:52.985
- Yeah, I had to learn how to be a lady.

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:54.713
(all laughing)

00:00:54.713 --> 00:00:57.590
'Cause, no, I didn't know, I didn't know.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:58.727
- I don't.
- I had to like,

00:00:58.727 --> 00:01:02.250
dab my face with a napkin and, you know,

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.835
you can't wipe your face like a monster!

00:01:04.835 --> 00:01:06.620
(all laughing)

00:01:06.620 --> 00:01:09.620
- Obviously I didn't attend
etiquette class (laughs).

00:01:09.620 --> 00:01:11.847
- Well, I still to this
day, people are like,

00:01:11.847 --> 00:01:13.277
"You should never eat in public,

00:01:13.277 --> 00:01:16.140
"'cause it's not great."
(all laughing)

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.440
- So what did your family think

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:18.750
whenever you told them you were gay?

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:19.583
'Cause, being from the South,

00:01:19.583 --> 00:01:21.400
that is not always an easy conversation.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.790
- Yeah, I mean, I think my mom,

00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:28.370
for her, she didn't want
my life to be harder than

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:31.230
what life can be, you know?
- Already?

00:01:31.230 --> 00:01:34.340
- Already, but we had this
really poignant moment,

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.290
I talk about it in my special,

00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:39.550
where I told her I was gay
and she was like stone-faced.

00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:42.265
And I was like, "Oh, man,
does she hate me now?"

00:01:42.265 --> 00:01:47.134
And she was like, "We
are goin' to Hooters."

00:01:47.134 --> 00:01:50.126
(all laughing)

00:01:50.126 --> 00:01:51.700
- I what's like, "What?"

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:53.780
- What?
- So that was her way

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.890
of being like, "I accept
you, let's go to Hooters."

00:01:56.890 --> 00:01:59.504
(all laughing)

00:01:59.504 --> 00:02:02.750
And then when I told my dad, he was like,

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:05.399
you know, he's a very typical Southern man

00:02:05.399 --> 00:02:07.347
that's very simple, and he's like,

00:02:07.347 --> 00:02:11.277
"Okay, all right, well, do you want us

00:02:11.277 --> 00:02:13.609
"to buy you a men's blazer?

00:02:13.609 --> 00:02:16.192
(all laughing)

00:02:17.187 --> 00:02:18.647
"Or a top hat?"

00:02:18.647 --> 00:02:20.087
(all laughing)

00:02:20.087 --> 00:02:21.120
What?

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:22.860
Lesbians don't wear top hats.

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:24.740
- I love it, but in his mind,

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.420
if women like men, then
you wanna dress like a man.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:29.690
- Sure, he's like, "Okay, let's get you

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:33.597
that top hat and blazer."
(all laughing)

